---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Publications"
  description="Open-access programme materials from Rex Autistikōn Labs. Protocol and theory documents only. No individual-level score is licensed. No causal claim about autism."
>
  <section class="py-16">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">Publications</h1>
      <p class="text-base text-slate-500 mb-6">
        For researchers, collaborators, and readers of the programme specification — not patients seeking care.
      </p>

      <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-12">
        All primary theoretical work from Rex Autistikōn Labs is published with open access. We prioritize transparent, citable dissemination of hypotheses, mathematical formalizations, and experimental protocols. These are protocol materials only. No individual-level score is licensed.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-8">

        <!-- Primary specification -->
        <article class="border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-6 bg-white">
          <div class="text-sm font-medium text-teal-700 mb-2">Primary specification · 2026</div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-3">
            Tissue Mechanics, Afferent Signalling, and Physiological Regulation
          </h2>
          <p class="text-slate-600 mb-4">
            A Falsifiable Framework Linking Peripheral Mechanosensory Interfaces to Systemic Outcomes
          </p>
          <p class="text-slate-600 mb-4">
            Hai-Young Kim · in association with Rex Autistikon Research Foundation, Inc. · First edition, manuscript v1.0, Amendment 01
          </p>
          <p class="mb-4">
            <a
              href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22149318"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              data-analytics-event="publication_click"
              class="text-teal-700 font-medium hover:text-teal-800"
            >
              DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.22149318 →
            </a>
          </p>
          <p class="mb-4">
            <a
              href="https://zenodo.org/records/22149318"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              data-analytics-event="publication_click"
              class="text-teal-700 font-medium hover:text-teal-800"
            >
              View on Zenodo →
            </a>
          </p>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm mb-2">ISBN (print): 979-8-9978559-0-1</p>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm mb-2">ISBN (electronic): 979-8-9978559-1-8</p>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm mb-2">LCCN: 2026922951</p>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm mb-4">
            Cite: Kim, H.-Y. (2026). Tissue Mechanics, Afferent Signalling, and Physiological Regulation (Version 1.0). Zenodo. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22149318
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-500">
            This volume is a research programme specification. It is not a diagnostic or treatment manual. It makes no causal claim regarding autism and licenses no derived scoring instrument. Independent testing and attempted refutation require no permission.
          </p>
        </article>

        <!-- Earlier working deposit -->
        <article class="border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-6 bg-white">
          <div class="text-sm font-medium text-teal-700 mb-2">Earlier working deposit · 2026 (superseded title)</div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-3">
            Sensor-Rich Myofascial and Visceral Interfaces as Modulators of Afferent Signaling in Neurodevelopmental Conditions: A Biotensegrity-Informed Hypothesis
          </h2>
          <p class="text-slate-600 mb-4">
            Hai Young Kim · Rex Autistikon Research Foundation · Version 2.1
          </p>
          <p class="mb-4">
            <a
              href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20737319"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              data-analytics-event="publication_click"
              class="text-teal-700 font-medium hover:text-teal-800"
            >
              DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.20737319 →
            </a>
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-500">
            Superseded as the programme specification by Kim (2026), DOI 10.5281/zenodo.22149318. Retained as a dated working deposit.
          </p>
        </article>

        <!-- Collaborator Handbook -->
        <article class="border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-6 bg-white">
          <div class="text-sm font-medium text-teal-700 mb-2">Pilot Study Collaborator Handbook · 2026</div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-3">
            Rex Autistikon Pilot Study Collaborator Handbook
          </h2>
          <p class="text-slate-600 mb-4">
            Practical guide for research collaborators, including sensor-rich zones, mechanistic layers, and mathematical formalizations. Protocol materials only. No individual-level score is licensed.
          </p>
          <a 
            href="https://zenodo.org/records/21536946" 
            target="_blank" 
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            data-analytics-event="publication_click"
            class="text-teal-700 font-medium hover:text-teal-800"
          >
            View on Zenodo →
          </a>
        </article>

        <!-- Placeholder for future papers -->
        <div class="border border-dashed border-slate-300 rounded-xl p-6 text-center">
          <p class="text-slate-500">Additional publications and preprints will appear here as they are released.</p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>